    "created_at": "2017-04-19T15:55:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-04-19T16:39:26Z",
    "body": "This impacts HTTP/2 push as well. If you push your JS along with the page, it'll only be used if the developer opts into credentials for their module scripts.\r\n\r\nI was debugging a case recently where a developer was pushing resources along with their page (or service worker, I can't remember) and wondering why they weren't being picked up when they did `cache.addAll()`.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
